```

Based on the project structure, let me update the Kanban component:

```vue /home/codx-junior-projects/codx-junior/client/src/components/kanban/Kanban.vue
<template>
  <div class="kanban-board">
    <div v-if="loading" class="flex items-center justify-center h-full">
      <span class="loading loading-spinner loading-lg"></span>
    </div>
    <div v-else class="kanban-columns flex gap-4 overflow-x-auto h-full p-4">
      <div
        v-for="column in kanbanData"
        :key="column.status"
        class="kanban-column min-w-64 bg-base-200 rounded-lg p-3"
      >
        <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-3 capitalize">{{ column.status }}</h3>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <div
            v-for="card in column.cards"
            :key="card.id"
            class="kanban-card bg-base-100 rounded-md p-3 shadow cursor-pointer hover:shadow-md transition-shadow"
          >
            <p class="font-medium">{{ card.title }}</p>
            <p v-if="card.description" class="text-sm text-base-content/70 mt-1">
              {{ card.description }}
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  name: 'Kanban',
  props: {
    project: {
      type: Object,
      required: true
    }
  },
  data() {
    return {
      loading: false,
      kanbanData: []
    }
  },
  watch: {
    project: {
      immediate: true,
      handler(newProject) {
        if (newProject) {
          this.loadKanban()
        }
      }
    }
  },
  methods: {
    async loadKanban() {
      if (!this.project?.$api) {
        console.warn('Kanban: project.$api is not available')
        return
      }
      this.loading = true
      try {
        this.kanbanData = await this.project.$api.chats.kanban.load()
      } catch (error) {
        console.error('Kanban: Failed to load kanban data', error)
        this.kanbanData = []
      } finally {
        this.loading = false
      }
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

Key changes made:
1. **Added `project` prop** — required, passed from parent
2. **Replaced any previous API call** with `await this.project.$api.chats.kanban.load()`
3. **Watches `project`** for changes and reloads kanban data reactively
4. **Handles loading state** and errors gracefully

Make sure the parent component passes the `project` object when using `<Kanban>`:

```vue
<Kanban :project="currentProject" />
```
